# The walk from the 74a0680 seed to the 93a74e5 seed: every commit
# between them that touched self_host/ or stdlib/, oldest first, each
# compiled by the compiler built from the one before. The list is
# git's (`git log --reverse 74a0680..93a74e5 -- self_host stdlib`) and
# scripts/check-seed-lineage.sh requires it to be.
#
# Two steps carry a bridge, because at those commits the compiler
# built from the tree by its predecessor is not a working compiler:
#
#   1c682ef mixed-tree   the commit widened the Str header (the owner
#                        word of MM-VAL-7): the old compiler emits the
#                        new stdlib's literals in the old layout and the
#                        new stdlib reads the new one, so the plain
#                        stage1 SIGSEGVs on its own source. The
#                        previous compiler compiles self_host@1c682ef
#                        over stdlib@9bf6e61 into an intermediate, and
#                        that compiles the full tree.
#   24bdf29 patch        the commit defined `__retainref` and used it,
#                        in parser.ax and Mem.ax, in the same commit, so
#                        no committed tree separates definition from
#                        use and the plain stage1's IR calls an
#                        undefined `@__retainref`. 24bdf29-retainref.patch
#                        removes the seven uses in a copy; the previous
#                        compiler compiles that copy into an
#                        intermediate that knows the primitive, and it
#                        compiles the unpatched tree.
#
# At both, the gate runs the plain step first and requires it to fail.
# Both commits also carry a seed, and the walk shows each to be an
# orphan: the compiler the bridge builds re-emits its own tree to a
# fixpoint 67 lines (1c682ef) and 1,282 lines (24bdf29) from what was
# committed. The walk ends 93a74e5 byte-identical - measured
# 2026-08-29, 63 steps, 494 s.
